{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nIn the live prompt-eval loop (`rebar.llm.evals.eval.run_eval` per dataset-bearing spec, the `eval-live` job in `.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml`), seven plan-review criterion specs fail some cases with:\n\n```\nreview result failed schema validation: 'dimension' is a required property\n```\n\nSpecs affected (case counts at `REBAR_EVAL_MAX_CASES=12`, 3 epochs, 5.5 run): plan-review-G7 (6), plan-review-ac-process-gate (2), plan-review-asserted-capability (5), plan-review-decomp-shape (2), plan-review-evidence-kind (14), plan-review-necessity (2), plan-review-no-file-impact (3). The same failure appears on origin/main 872e7f6c3fd with Opus 4.8 / Sonnet 4.6, so it is not model-specific.\n\n## Root cause (reproduced offline 2026-11-17, origin/main 05c6414358f)\n\nThe deterministic scorer `emits_valid_findings` is registered as `_schema_review_result` (`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_scorers.py:425`, `:160`), which validates the output against the `review_result` schema via `findings.validate_result` (`src/rebar/llm/findings.py:134`). That schema requires `dimension` on each finding.\n\nThe seven affected specs are criterion-id specs: `_criterion_id` (`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py:76`) resolves their prompt id to a registry criterion, so `run_case` solves them with the criterion arm (`eval_solver.py:101`), which returns Pass-1 findings in the `plan_review_findings` contract shape (`finding`, `criteria`, `evidence`, ... — `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py:46` `_pass1_model`), never `dimension`. The spec files describe the scorer as \"validates against the plan_review_findings contract\". `pass1_chunk`/`pass1_container` normalize each model finding before it reaches the scorer (`passes.py:284-301`, `:379-412`): `finding` is coerced with `f.get(\"finding\", \"\")`, and findings with no in-set criterion are dropped.\n\nEvery other consumer of the scorer name is also a criterion-id spec that goes through the criterion arm and emits the Pass-1 shape, so none needs an edit and all benefit: the gate fixture specs `evals/plan-review-gate/fixtures/eval_specs/*.eval.yaml`, the repo-overlay project specs `.rebar/evals/plan-review-project-*.eval.yaml` (dotted `project.*` ids), and every spec `src/rebar/llm/evals/fixture_emit.py` generates (its scorer template names `emits_valid_findings`). The three PASS-named packaged specs that list it (plan-review-container, -finder, -isf-finder) raise \"no eval solver\" today (`eval_solver.py:423`); routing them is sibling bug `knightly-salty-orangutan`, and they emit the same Pass-1 shape once routed.\n\nReproduction: `eval_solver.run_case(\"plan-review-G7\", <a G7 must-fire case>, runner=FakeRunner(findings=[{\"finding\": \"x\", \"criteria\": [\"G7\"], \"evidence\": [\"q\"]}]))` then `score(\"emits_valid_findings\", ...)` -> `passed=False, \"'dimension' is a required property\"`. With no findings it passes, which is why only the cases where the finder fired were lost.\n\nThe same shape mismatch affects `attributes_g3_vs_g4` (`_attributes_criterion`, `eval_scorers.py:287`), used only by plan-review-container: it searches the finding keys `criterion`/`dimension`/`title`/`detail`, but Pass-1 container findings carry the attribution in the `criteria` list, so a correctly attributed G3/G4 finding scores as unattributed once the container spec runs (after the sibling fix).\n\n## Approach\n\nScore plan-review criterion output against the contract it is produced under, reusing the registered Pass-1 model rather than re-describing it:\n\n1. Add `_schema_plan_review_findings` in `eval_scorers.py`. Inside the function it imports `rebar.llm.plan_review.passes` and calls `passes.register_contracts()` (idempotent, `passes.py:120`) before `contracts.response_model_for(\"plan_review_findings\")`, so validation never silently falls back to the review_result model (`contracts.py:38-40`). It fails when: the output is not a dict; `findings` is absent or not a list; the model rejects it (pydantic error message); or any finding's `finding` text is empty after `strip()` (the normalized shape coerces a missing `finding` to `\"\"`, so this is what catches a model that emitted no claim).\n2. Register `emits_valid_findings` to that scorer. `emits_valid_review_result` keeps `_schema_review_result` for the specs that really emit `review_result` (code-quality, spec-alignment).\n3. `_attributes_criterion` also credits a finding whose `criteria` list contains the case's criterion, by exact case-insensitive element match (so `G3` never matches `G33`, and `g3` matches `G3`). A finding listing both G3 and G4 is credited to each. The existing substring match over `criterion`/`dimension`/`title`/`detail` is kept unchanged; a finding is credited if either source matches.\n\nNo config key, env var or flag is added.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_scorers.py` — new scorer, registry entry, attribution read.\n- `tests/unit/test_eval_scorers.py` — offline tests.\n- `tests/unit/test_eval.py` — the existing `run_eval` tests inject a `solve` that returns review_result-shaped findings (`severity`/`dimension`/`detail`) for the `plan-review-finder` spec, so they reach `emits_valid_findings` directly, without `run_case`. They are migrated to the Pass-1 shape (`{\"finding\": ..., \"criteria\": [...]}`) so they keep asserting the gate passes.\n\nPortability: pure in-process validation; no subprocess, file descriptor, signal or path handling. The fresh-interpreter test runs `sys.executable` with an argument list (no shell).\n\n## Testing\n\nOffline, no model:\n- happy path, parametrized over the packaged criterion-id specs that list `emits_valid_findings`; the test first asserts the discovered set equals exactly {plan-review-G7, -ac-process-gate, -asserted-capability, -decomp-shape, -evidence-kind, -necessity, -no-file-impact}. For each, `run_case` on one must-fire case with a `FakeRunner` returning a fired finding for that criterion, then `emits_valid_findings` passes and no message contains `dimension`. An empty `findings` list passes.\n- self-registration: a fresh interpreter (`subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-c\", ...])`) imports `eval_scorers`, asserts `\"rebar.llm.plan_review.passes\" not in sys.modules`, scores a hand-built Pass-1 output with `emits_valid_findings`, and asserts it passes (a review_result fallback would reject it for missing `dimension`).\n- failure path: a review_result-shaped finding (`dimension`, no `finding`), a finding whose `finding` is empty, an output whose `findings` is not a list, and a non-dict output each fail `emits_valid_findings`.\n- attribution: one positive end-to-end case built through `eval_solver.run_case(\"plan-review-container\", <the first G3 must-fire case of the packaged container spec, which carries `children`>, runner=FakeRunner(...G3 finding...))` once the sibling arm exists, otherwise `run_case(\"G3\", <same case>)` (the criterion arm routes a G3 case with `children` through `passes.pass1_container`) — credited to G3. Then direct scorer calls on hand-built `{\"findings\": [{\"finding\": \"x\", \"criteria\": [...]}]}` outputs: `[\"G4\"]` on a G3 case fails; `[\"G3\", \"G4\"]` passes on both a G3 case and a G4 case; `[\"G33\"]` on a G3 case fails; `[\"g3\"]` on a G3 case passes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `emits_valid_findings` validates the `plan_review_findings` contract: for each of the seven criterion-id specs, a fired Pass-1 finding from the criterion arm passes and no \"'dimension' is a required property\" error occurs; checked by a parametrized unit test in `tests/unit/test_eval_scorers.py` (with an exact discovered-set assertion) that fails on origin/main 05c6414358f.\n- [ ] The scorer registers the contract itself (fresh-interpreter test passes with `passes` not preloaded) and still fails malformed output: review_result-shaped finding, empty `finding` text, non-list `findings`, non-dict; checked by unit tests.\n- [ ] `attributes_g3_vs_g4` credits attribution carried in a finding's `criteria` list by exact case-insensitive element match: G3 credited, G4-only rejected on a G3 case, `[\"G3\",\"G4\"]` credited on both, `G33` rejected, `g3` credited; checked by unit tests.\n- [ ] The migrated `tests/unit/test_eval.py` `run_eval` tests pass under the new scorer, and `emits_valid_review_result` is unchanged (existing tests pass).\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794970659874224917,"uuid":"9ea52629-f22a-4502-b4bd-eca1b49d0a5a"}